from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
base=Path('/data/coding/scanweave/qualification/acr06');e=base/'ink37';p=e/'polarity37';loc=base/'local/ink37/polarity37'
rows=json.loads((p/'measurements.json').read_text());corpus=[x for x in rows if x['set']=='corpus'];controls=[x for x in rows if x['set']!='corpus'];assert len(corpus)==32
inverted={('historical',n) for n in range(1,6)}|{('receipts',n) for n in (4,6,7,8,9)}
f=lambda v:'—' if v is None else f'{v:.4f}'
lookup={(x['document'],int(x['page_id'][1:])):x for x in corpus}
def row(doc,n):return lookup[(doc,n)]
def size(path):return path.stat().st_size
a=row('historical',4);b=row('forms',1);r4=row('receipts',4);r6=row('receipts',6);r9=row('receipts',9)
lines=['# Issue 37 — OCR foreground-fraction qualification','', '**Status: the requested statistic does not separate normal and inverted pages. In accordance with the instruction to stop in this case, no routing change, candidate, commit, push or PR was made.** The instrumented conversion uses the unchanged main segmentation and output assembly; its PDFs matched the previously reproduced main hashes.','', '## Method','', 'At main `9655fccc1b9e2ce479dd95d06b5f48ea2bfc0e6d`, build `cargo build --release --locked -p scanweave-cli` and run the five group sources at `--dpi 300 --profile clearscan --glyph-sharing off`. The temporary [instrumentation](polarity37/instrumentation.patch) records each actual `input.spans[].symbols[]` polygon’s bounding rectangle, rounded outward and clipped to the page, immediately after `segment()`; it counts foreground bits and total pixels in the exact input raster. Invalid or empty boxes are omitted. The [summary script](polarity37/summarize.py) calculates the median and linearly interpolated p10/p90. [Per-page statistics and links to every per-box count](polarity37/measurements.json) are supplied. Luminance is 0–255 Rec. 709-weighted RGB.','', '## Separation result','',f"Historical page 4 is an inverted page with {a['box_count']} boxes and median **{a['median']:.4f}**; forms page 1 has normal polarity, {b['box_count']} boxes and median **{b['median']:.4f}**. Any rule that flags high medians and catches the former also flags the latter. This overlap is independent of how a too-few-box case is handled.",f"The known inverted receipts also violate the expected high-median assumption: receipts 4 has {r4['box_count']} boxes and median {f(r4['median'])}; receipts 6 has {r6['box_count']} boxes and median {f(r6['median'])}; receipts 9 has {r9['box_count']} boxes and median {f(r9['median'])}. See the page table for ranges and zero-box pages.",'', 'The control set supplies additional counterexamples; none were used to choose a threshold. The positive reverse-panel case `reverse_panel-72` has 25 visible vectors and its measured page median is given below. Several synthetic fully reverse pages have OCR-box medians above 0.5, while the 72-pixel reverse panel has a lower median. These controls show that the proportion is affected by OCR box geometry, character shapes, and mixed content. The true reverse-page variants in the frozen set emitted no visible vectors, so they do not constitute the requested positive true-reverse-vector control. The source-derived contextual dark-table control emitted seven vectors, but is derived from the same receipt corpus and is not independent truth.','', 'No threshold is chosen: there is no gap in the real-page data, and the user explicitly directed us to stop rather than route if the statistic cannot separate normal and inverted pages. Thus every page’s decision is **not applied**, with reason **no separating threshold**. No claim is made that a more complex classifier cannot exist.',
'For the two zero-box corpus pages, the requested special case would retain existing behavior for receipts 1 (ink darker than paper) and select `raster_baseline` for receipts 7 (ink lighter than paper). These are the requested hypothetical routes only; neither was applied because the overall decision rule failed. No cutoff for a nonzero but insufficient box count was selected.','', '## Real pages','', 'Paper and ink are main’s existing estimates. “Majority” counts OCR boxes with foreground fraction greater than 0.5. A dash means zero valid boxes.','', '| Page | Existing polarity | Boxes | Median | p10–p90 | Majority | Paper RGB / L | Ink RGB / L | Decision |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|']
for x in corpus:
 n=int(x['page_id'][1:]);lab='inverted' if (x['document'],n) in inverted else 'other'
 lines.append(f"| {x['document']} {n} | {lab} | {x['box_count']} | {f(x['median'])} | {f(x['p10'])}–{f(x['p90'])} | {x['majority_boxes']} | {x['paper']} / {x['paper_luminance']:.2f} | {x['ink']} / {x['ink_luminance']:.2f} | not applied |")
lines+=['','## Frozen controls','', 'The existing [seed 370611 set](controls-truth.json), [supplemental set](supplemental-truth.json), [positive variants](positive-controls-truth.json), [dark-table variants](table-candidates-truth.json), and [contextual receipt control](table-context-truth.json) were measured unchanged. The recorded [DejaVu licence](DejaVu-LICENSE.txt) applies to the synthetic text.','', '| Set / case | Page | Boxes | Median | p10–p90 | Majority | Paper RGB / L | Ink RGB / L |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|']
for x in controls:
 n=int(x['page_id'][1:]);lines.append(f"| {x['set']} / {x['document']} | {n} | {x['box_count']} | {f(x['median'])} | {f(x['p10'])}–{f(x['p90'])} | {x['majority_boxes']} | {x['paper']} / {x['paper_luminance']:.2f} | {x['ink']} / {x['ink_luminance']:.2f} |")
lines+=['','## Output identity and checks','', 'The instrumented main reruns matched the previous fresh-main document hashes; they do not constitute a candidate.']
for name in ('historical','financial','mixed','receipts','forms'):
 path=loc/f'{name}-main.pdf'; h=hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest();lines.append(f'- {name}: `{h}`, {size(path):,} bytes.')
lines+=['','Because routing was not implemented, there are no candidate page hashes, SSIM, pixel diffs, extraction/search comparisons, qpdf/OTS results, unit tests or candidate CI gates. The existing [65-glyph panel index](glyph-panel-index.json) and [automated review](glyph-review.txt) belong to an earlier rejected prototype and are not evidence for a candidate under this design. The earlier [glyph-mask measurement report](REPORT-glyph-mask.md) and rejected fallback experiments remain as history. The original issue’s 65 affected visible objects and ten inverted pages are documented there.','', '## Limitations','', 'This measures rectangular OCR-symbol boxes, including small and overlapping boxes, rather than ground-truth character segmentation. Some pages have no or very few OCR symbols; those cannot yield a robust median and are indicated explicitly. There is no separately established true reverse page that emits light visible vectors. The mixed-polarity panel cannot be reliably identified from this page median alone. The experiment leaves donors, glyph sharing, auto mode, ownership, coverage, text and segmentation untouched, so it does not assess the consequences of changing them.','', 'The temporary instrumentation was removed after all jobs completed. The product worktree is clean; no commit or push was made.','']
(e/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
